## Inputs a verifier in 2106 would need

This means verifying historical V1 receipts in 2106, not extending the issuance
window to 2106. Current wall-clock expiry, revocation, algorithm prohibitions and
service availability must not silently overwrite the frozen V1 verdict
(`docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:253-278`). No live fetch is an offline input.

| Input to preserve/distribute | What the documents supply | What they do not say how to obtain or format |
|---|---|---|
| **Authenticated trust configuration** | Distributed with verifier, never from bundle; D=wamason.com, root KSKs, repository keys/intervals, parameters, pins; append-only entries and finalized endpoints (`docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:152-155`, `:221-223`, `:324-332`; `docs/V1-PROFILE.md:209-219`). | Concrete configuration bytes/schema, authentication root/package procedure, update chain, version selection, open-end convention and provenance archive. A9 requires repository entries with D, key and inclusive signing interval; P's simpler pair is insufficient on its own. Must retain original configuration for exact declared-input reproducibility; augmented coverage can legitimately improve an earlier UNVERIFIABLE result. |
| **Header pins and historical raw headers** | Signed/versioned mainnet hashes, every supplied header pinned, uncovered history UNVERIFIABLE (`docs/V1-PROFILE.md:274-277`, `:387-392`). | Signer key, signature format/signed preimage, height/hash/byte-order schema, required heights/depth coverage, authentic acquisition process and successor/confirmation-time representation. Hashes without reconstructible header bytes do not give header timestamps. |
| **Root KSKs and lifetimes** | KSK-2017/2024, separate signing/reliance/publication/revocation periods; interval [signing-start, signing-end+L], L sourced/observed; some dates and L=21d in P (`docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:307-323`; `docs/V1-PROFILE.md:221-251`). | Actual DNSKEY/public-key bytes, encoding and authentic source archive; complete period starts/end representations and cited validity evidence in the allowed set. Names/key tags alone are not trust anchors. Historical RRSIG evaluation needs the relevant DNSSEC time/serial rules. Retain old KSKs; do not replace them with whatever key is current in 2106. |
| **Bundle container and all evidence bytes** | Twelve-member proposed inventory, tagged frames/A_sig/snapshot envelope, raw spec/vectors/preamble hash binding (`docs/V1-PROFILE.md:91-116`; `formal/p8/ENCODING-V1.md:71-72`, `:493-506`, `:536-540`). | Container/transport schema, names/order/duplicate handling, layer/request fields, key and possession-signature packaging, snapshot-body format, OTS/txid/header/confirmation packaging. Need exact signature bytes; normalized/re-signed copies cannot inherit the old stamp. |
| **Governing V1 specification and branch** | Signed id/hash; baseline plus conditional hybrid supplement; frozen policy applies later (`docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:146-148`, `:268-278`, `:386-391`). | Frozen specification object bytes/hash, branch choice/pair id/context, trusted supported-spec catalog and delivery/authentication mechanism. Do not obtain executable verifier policy from a receipt's self-supplied document alone. |
| **Repository authority material** | Pinned D/key, raw signed sha1 commit/tree/blob path, exact `object_format="sha1"`, stamped 40 lowercase hex+LF, fixed path/modes, inclusive key interval (`docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:295-305`, `:324-328`; `docs/V1-PROFILE.md:329-341`). | Actual repository public key(s), complete signing intervals/provenance, key serialization, object container association and signature profile; full git grammar/armour dependencies. Authentic historical evidence can be archived; network proof of public publication is not a verifier requirement. |
| **Normative dependency closure** | Eight named dependency families; possible seven fields and extra standards unresolved (`docs/V1-PROFILE.md:427-450`; `formal/p8/PROOF.md:95-110`). | Exact editions/sections/errata, retrievable redistributed bytes/digests and complete offline definitions for ES number formatting, Unicode 16/NFC, OpenPGP, DNSSEC, OTS, Bitcoin and git. Citations to standards are useful dependencies, not a complete bundled archival input format. |

## Verification evidence and limits

The local probes were written from these documents and constructed synthetic
objects. They use no project vectors or existing signatures. Synthetic rule-O
MPIs establish syntax only, not ECDSA validity; unknown-algorithm opaque strings
establish only the allowed codec route. Changed syntactically admissible signature
bytes change the anchor digest; this is not a demonstrated OTS verification.

