   697	  `check.py` `date_ok` and `is_domain`, and the same in `gen.py` through `datetime`.
   698	- **Rationale.** It codifies what both codecs already do, so no vector changes. **No longer verdict-affecting for
   699	  V1:** G34 forces `issuer` = `wamason.com`. And any declared time or window outside the uint32 nTime range fails a
   700	  conjunct or the window rule with `INVALID` under either reading.
   701	
   702	---
   703	
   704	## I. Aggregation and reasons: G26 (and G31, G30, G32 in §J)
   705	
   706	### G26: all-failure aggregation
   707	
   708	- **Resolution.**
   709	  - A verifier **may stop early only on a failed check**, since `INVALID` is final.
   710	  - Otherwise it evaluates every check whose inputs exist:
   711	    - a check whose input is **unperformable** is unperformable;
   712	    - a check that depends on a **failed** check is not evaluated (the verdict is already `INVALID`);
   713	    - checks that do not depend on either keep running.
   714	  - **Input-independent checks**, which always run when their bytes are present: the codecs; the time-free
   715	    cryptographic validity of RRSIGs; DNS record grammar; git grammar and ids; manifest and key binding.
   716	  - **Checks that depend on time inputs:** RRSIG windows, KSK reliance and repository intervals (on T_snap or T_git);
   717	    the conjuncts and the window rule (on T).
   718	  - **The unknown `alg` case** routes the slot as opaque (Lemma 7a) and continues.
   719	  - **Verdict:** any failed → `INVALID`; else any unperformable → `UNVERIFIABLE`; else `VALID_STRICT` (R-2.26).
   720	- **Rationale.** The verdict is then independent of evaluation order (SPEC R-5.16), and GAPS's short-circuit fork
   721	  (unknown `alg` hiding a bad slot) is closed.
   722	
   723	---
   724	
   725	## J. The non-verdict rows (briefly)
   726	
   727	| Gap | Resolution | Label | Lands |
   728	|---|---|---|---|
   729	| G30 | An empty snapshot body, or a payload over its cap, gives `LENGTH_CAP`, checked before the JSON categories. This matches E§1.4 and §6 | CLARIFY | P §3.2 |
   730	| G31 | The reported reason is the first failed check in this stage order, or if none failed, the first unperformable one: dispatch → container → `a_sig` codec (E order) → manifest → keys → receipt consistency → `alg` → profile constants (issuer, spec, binding forms) → signatures and possession → receipt OTS, headers and txid → conjuncts → snapshot (format, OTS, DNSSEC, record E§7 order, time) → git (format, ids, path, signature, OTS, interval, after-issue) → channel equality → `ISSUANCE_WINDOW` → bundle-object hashes. **This matters even though it is not verdict-affecting**: the reason code is one of A9.4's six stable fields, which later verifiers must reproduce | CLARIFY | P §3.2 |
   731	| G32 | Report = JCS object `{"historical_security":"NOT_EVALUATED", "reason", "revocation":"NOT_EVALUATED", "standing":"ABSENT/NOT_ISSUED_IN_PROFILE", "T", "verdict"}`. The success reason is `OK`. T is an RFC 3339 string when the receipt proof matches `A_sig` and has a qualifying attestation, and `null` otherwise. Diagnostics (config version and hash, spec hash, per-check list) sit outside the stable six | CLARIFY | P §3.4 |
   732	| G33 | The container's `issuer_record` (R-3.46, registered) holds `policy_version` and `observed_anchor_delay_s` as strings. It is checked against the schema only and never affects the verdict | CLARIFY | P §2.1 |
   733	| G35 | Witness order (key tag, inception, expiration, signature bytes), first that validates, becomes the frozen rule. It changes no verdict and makes the reported witness deterministic | CLARIFY | P §7.3 |
   734	| G36 | "Repository key = offline root" is an operating fact (runbook), not verifier policy. Close the OPEN that way | CLARIFY | P §5 |
   735	| G37 | The baseline is the frozen spec object hash in the catalog (G13), not the draft labels | CLARIFY | P §1 |
   736	| G38 | Delete the stale "needs an author sentence" remarks (E:147-148, D-1; PROOF §6 last bullet); A9.8 governs | CLARIFY | E, R wording |
   737	| G39 | Re-extract P §6 from A9.5 and A9.6: SHA-1 descriptor, 40 hex + LF, repository intervals, per-receipt window. No verifier non-overlap check | CLARIFY | P §6 |
   738	
   739	---
   740	
   741	## K. For the author and owner
   742	
   743	**Needs an amendment:** none. Every resolution sits in the unregistered profile (P) or in wording of ENCODING-V1,
   744	which is DRAFT. No signed byte changes, and no P8 vector changes.
